{"kind":"assert","text":"Re-filed with a live basis. My first attempt rested on my promise 22a0df9c, which your merge 6bb01a86 world-staled between my writing it and the write boundary reading it. Ordinary staleness, restating rather than overriding.\n\nTHE SCOPE QUESTION. docs/reference/gs/serve.md lines 272 to 274 say: \"The remote is read from the repository's own configuration only — `git config --local` — so configuration outside the repository cannot say where the repository lives.\" That is the defect's own false reasoning, stated more strongly on this page than the architecture page stated it. Your conditions on 3b06d237 name architecture.md for correction and do not name serve.md.\n\nYour ruling at 85453083 on the other lane states the principle I would apply — a path already in the lane's artifact set is in scope, and the head moves once rather than in rounds. serve.md is in the remote-link seven-path set too. I am asking rather than extrapolating from a ruling you made about a different row, because on this lane I have three times decided for myself what was implied. If the principle carries, say so and it lands in the same recut.\n\nThe concrete reason it matters: if I publish an artifact at serve.md standing at a head where that sentence remains, the artifact is false when I sign it.\n\nTHE HEAD NEEDS RECUTTING ANYWAY, which changes the cost of your answer to nearly nothing. Merge 6bb01a86 moved main to c679fb73 and touched ui/, internal/app/app_test.go, internal/service/uidist and docs/reference/architecture.md — four of this lane's seven paths. My implementation head 3f174893 no longer merges cleanly. So the head moves regardless, and folding serve.md into that move costs one sentence rather than a round.\n\nWHERE THE WORK STANDS. The repair itself is built and gated at 3f174893 against the old base: five redirectable call sites in internal/app rather than the one codex named, each separately mutation-covered, plus the raw-delimiter fix. I have not published artifacts and have not requested review, because the base moved under it and because I have not yet watched the gates exit at a final head with my own hand. I will re-run them at whatever the recut produces and report those numbers, not the ones from the superseded base.\n\nFINDING WORTH CARRYING INTO THE RECUT, which I reported before the staleness and will restate so it is not lost: GIT_LITERAL_PATHSPECS and GIT_NOGLOB_PATHSPECS turn citingDocuments' `*.md` pathspec into a literal filename matching nothing, so the citation gate returns empty and a cited retirement lands. That is a guard bypass rather than a display defect, and it is fixed alongside the routing family."}